    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d333">

                <pb facs="0343" n="331" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg331"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Stettinius Mission/73: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-27T17:00:00+02:00">April 27, 1944—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 27—3:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>3446. Deles 36. From the Under Secretary. I discussed the question of Iran
                    yesterday with Eden and the Soviet Ambassador, on the lines indicated in Deles
                    number 22, April 19, after Murray and Sir Maurice had paved the way by a similar
                    talk with the Counselor of the Soviet Embassy. The Soviet reaction was favorable
                    in both instances and the Ambassador is telegraphing Moscow as requested.</p>
                <p>I suggest that appropriate instructions be sent to Ford without delay and that
                    Moscow be informed of these developments.<anchor n="65" xml:id="d333-f1"/> The
                    British are telegraphing their representatives at Tehran and Moscow today.
                    [Stettinius.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d333-f1" n="65" xml:id="d333-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated in paraphrase in telegram 261, April 28, 5 p.m., to Tehran, and in
                    telegram 1058, 5 p.m., to Moscow.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
